# 7. Preprocessing (Page 3)
old_prep = 'automated preprocessing pipeline: (1) <i>Data Ingestion and Cleaning:</i> Artifacts, sensor dropouts, and non-physiological outliers (e.g., negative blood pressures, SpO2 &gt; 100%) were filtered; (2) <i>Missing-Value Handling:</i> Median imputation fitted strictly on training data partitions was applied to numeric features, while missing categorical values were mapped to a distinct missing indicator; (3) <i>Temporal Aggregation:</i> For telemetry data, 5-minute rolling windows [t - 300s, t] were aggregated using backward summary statistics (mean, median, standard deviation, minimum, maximum, linear slope); (4) <i>ECG Beat Segmentation:</i> ECG channels were filtered using bandpass filtering (0.5–40 Hz), with R-peaks detected via Pan-Tompkins algorithm, extracting 360-sample windows (-150 to +210 samples around R-peaks); (5) <i>Sequence Construction:</i> Inpatient temporal lab and vital sequences were padded to standardized sequence lengths (seq_len=24) with masking layers for recurrent deep networks; and (6) <i>Target-Definition Review:</i> Ground truth clinical targets were cross-referenced against published clinical consensus definitions (e.g., MAP &lt; 65 mmHg for Hypotension, SpO2 &lt; 90% for Hypoxia, HR &lt; 60 bpm for Bradycardia, HR &gt; 100 bpm for Tachycardia).'
new_prep = 'automated preprocessing pipeline: <i>Data Ingestion and Cleaning:</i> Artifacts, sensor dropouts, and non-physiological outliers (e.g., negative blood pressures, SpO2 &gt; 100%) were filtered; <i>Missing-Value Handling:</i> Median imputation fitted strictly on training data partitions was applied to numeric features, while missing categorical values were mapped to a distinct missing indicator; <i>Temporal Aggregation:</i> For telemetry data, 5-minute rolling windows [t - 300s, t] were aggregated using backward summary statistics (mean, median, standard deviation, minimum, maximum, linear slope); <i>ECG Beat Segmentation:</i> ECG channels were filtered using bandpass filtering (0.5–40 Hz), with R-peaks detected via Pan-Tompkins algorithm, extracting 360-sample windows (-150 to +210 samples around R-peaks); <i>Sequence Construction:</i> Inpatient temporal lab and vital sequences were padded to standardized sequence lengths (seq_len=24) with masking layers for recurrent deep networks; and <i>Target-Definition Review:</i> Ground truth clinical targets were cross-referenced against published clinical consensus definitions (e.g., MAP &lt; 65 mmHg for Hypotension, SpO2 &lt; 90% for Hypoxia, HR &lt; 60 bpm for Bradycardia, HR &gt; 100 bpm for Tachycardia).'
