# 8. Leakage (Page 3)
old_leak = 'enforced across all models: (1) <i>Patient/Record Grouped Partitioning:</i> Data was partitioned into 70% Training, 15% Validation, and 15% Frozen Test cohorts strictly grouped by patient or record identifiers (caseid in VitalDB, subject_id in MIMIC-IV and MIMIC-IV-ED, and record_id in MIT-BIH), ensuring zero patient overlap such that P_train &cap; P_val = &empty; and P_train &cap; P_test = &empty;; (2) <i>Target-Defining Feature Purging:</i> Features that mechanically define target outcomes were permanently removed: continuous invasive arterial pressures were purged from Hypotension; continuous SpO2 was purged from Hypoxia; heart rate indicators were purged from Bradycardia and Tachycardia; emergency triage acuity scores were purged from Emergency Severity; and post-admission laboratory measurements and hospital length-of-stay metrics were purged from inpatient models; (3) <i>Train-Only Preprocessing Parameter Fitting:</i> Imputation medians, frequency tables, and StandardScaler parameters were computed exclusively on training partitions and applied without alteration to validation and test partitions; (4) <i>Pre-Outcome Backward Rolling Windows:</i> All telemetry summary statistics were computed backward across [t - 300s, t] without forward-looking temporal leakage; and (5) <i>Single-Touch Frozen Evaluation:</i> The test sets were held completely untouched during feature engineering, model architecture exploration, and hyperparameter tuning; optimal decision thresholds were selected on validation Precision-Recall curves and subsequently evaluated once on the frozen test sets.'
new_leak = 'enforced across all models: <i>Patient/Record Grouped Partitioning:</i> Data was partitioned into 70% Training, 15% Validation, and 15% Frozen Test cohorts strictly grouped by patient or record identifiers (caseid in VitalDB, subject_id in MIMIC-IV and MIMIC-IV-ED, and record_id in MIT-BIH), ensuring zero patient overlap such that P_train &cap; P_val = &empty; and P_train &cap; P_test = &empty;; <i>Target-Defining Feature Purging:</i> Features that mechanically define target outcomes were permanently removed: continuous invasive arterial pressures were purged from Hypotension; continuous SpO2 was purged from Hypoxia; heart rate indicators were purged from Bradycardia and Tachycardia; emergency triage acuity scores were purged from Emergency Severity; and post-admission laboratory measurements and hospital length-of-stay metrics were purged from inpatient models; <i>Train-Only Preprocessing Parameter Fitting:</i> Imputation medians, frequency tables, and StandardScaler parameters were computed exclusively on training partitions and applied without alteration to validation and test partitions; <i>Pre-Outcome Backward Rolling Windows:</i> All telemetry summary statistics were computed backward across [t - 300s, t] without forward-looking temporal leakage; and <i>Single-Touch Frozen Evaluation:</i> The test sets were held completely untouched during feature engineering, model architecture exploration, and hyperparameter tuning; optimal decision thresholds were selected on validation Precision-Recall curves and subsequently evaluated once on the frozen test sets.'
