old_archs = 'matched to specific data structures (Table III): (1) <i>HistGradientBoosting:</i> Selected for Hypotension, Hypoxia, and Tachycardia due to its native handling of missing values, rapid inference latency, and robust leaf-wise histogram binning across continuous surgical telemetry vectors comprising backward rolling summary statistics (mean, median, standard deviation, min, max, linear slope over 5-minute windows [t - 300s, t]); (2) <i>LightGBM:</i> Deployed for Arrhythmia Detection and Fluid Recommendation, providing fast leaf-wise tree growth, native categorical support, exact TreeSHAP attribution compatibility, and strong probability calibration across high-dimensional feature spaces; (3) <i>CatBoost:</i> Selected for Emergency Severity Assessment due to its specialized handling of high-cardinality categorical variables (chief complaints, arrival modes, insurance types) using ordered target encoding and symmetric oblivious decision trees that resist overfitting; (4) <i>ClinicalCNN (1D-CNN):</i> Engineered for Bradycardia telemetry classification, employing three 1D convolutional layers (kernel sizes 3 and 5, filter depth 64–128) with batch normalization, ReLU activation, max-pooling, and dropout (0.25) to capture localized morphological waveform shifts; (5) <i>ClinicalLSTM:</i> Deployed for Surgical Blood Loss prediction, utilizing a two-layer bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory network (hidden dimension 64, dropout 0.20) to capture cumulative fluid shift dependencies; and (6) <i>ClinicalGRU:</i> Utilized for ICU Admission and In-Hospital Mortality, leveraging a two-layer Gated Recurrent Unit network (hidden dimension 64, dropout 0.20) with masked loss functions for efficient sequential learning over irregularly sampled inpatient laboratory trajectories (seq_len=24).'
