old_lim = 'several key limitations must be emphasized: (1) All ten prediction models were trained and benchmarked on retrospective observational cohorts (VitalDB from South Korea, MIT-BIH, and MIMIC-IV from the United States); differences in institutional protocols, surgical case mix, patient genetics, and drug administration habits across international hospitals may induce domain shift; (2) Anesth AI is developed strictly as an academic research decision-support prototype and has not received regulatory clearance (such as FDA 510(k) or CE mark) as a commercial medical device; (3) The platform has not undergone prospective randomized controlled clinical trial evaluation; (4) In highly imbalanced tasks such as Hypoxia (0.99% prevalence) and In-Hospital Mortality (2.22% prevalence), positive predictive value remains modest despite high specificity, requiring clinicians to interpret flags within holistic clinical context; (5) High-frequency operating theater ECG telemetry is susceptible to surgical electrocautery and motion artifacts that differ from clean ambulatory Holter recordings; and (6) The system does not replace attending clinical judgment; all calculations, risk scores, and checklists require explicit attending confirmation.'
